# LinkedParticles — permanent identifiers for the LinkedParticles epistemic
# knowledge standard (https://github.com/LinkedParticles).
#
# The standard's normative artifacts (JSON Schema, JSON-LD @context, five SHACL
# shapes) declare their $id / vocabulary IRIs under https://w3id.org/linkedparticles/.
# The IRIs are the stable identity; the hosting below is expected to move, which
# is the whole reason this indirection exists (ADR 0157).
#
# Maintainer: LinkedParticles (https://github.com/LinkedParticles)

Options +FollowSymLinks
RewriteEngine on

# PARKED PHASE (current). The standard repository is not public yet, so every
# path under the namespace 302s to the organization landing page rather than
# 404-ing. 302 (not 301) is deliberate: the target changes the moment the
# standard repo publishes, and a cached 301 would be very hard to undo.
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://github.com/LinkedParticles [R=302,L]

# SERVING PHASE (follow-up PR, once the standard repo's GitHub Pages site is
# live). Replace the rule above with the path-preserving rule below so that
# https://w3id.org/linkedparticles/schemas/particle.schema.json resolves to the
# published artifact, and content negotiation serves RDF to Linked Data clients.
#
# RewriteRule ^$ https://linkedparticles.github.io/particles-standard/ [R=302,L]
# RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://linkedparticles.github.io/particles-standard/$1 [R=302,L]
